{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"bonfire","model_identifier":"bonfire","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# bonfire\n\nBonfire (light, Patch 2; real model in Patch 5): a ring of rough stones round a tall tepee of split logs, with glowing embers inside, a stack of spare logs and a stump with an axe. No spit or pot, so it reads as a light and not a cooking fire.\n\n- Footprint: 3 x 3 columns (48 x 48 units, 1.35 x 1.35 m), centred on the origin, front faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -23..24, y 0..46, z -24..23 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material.\n- Cubes: finished 63, construction_0 15, construction_33 10, construction_66 5, ruined 21 (the state sets are cut from the finished cubes and map into the texture regions of the faces they were cut from).\n- Glowing parts: `glow_core` and `glow_ember_*`.\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and footing with materials waiting, then walls rising inside scaffold).\n- `ruined`: broken walls at uneven heights, rubble and fallen beams.\n- `bonfire_damaged.png`: damaged texture (cracks, scorch) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 44 x 46 x 44 centred at the origin (the stone ring and the tepee).\n\n## Effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `fx_fire` at (0, 10, 0): where the flames start, inside the tepee.\n- `fx_smoke` at (0, 44, 0): the tepee tip."},"resolution":{"width":256,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"rock_stone_01","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[13.25,0,0.1],"to":[20.83,6.